cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MarketTickStreamer.jl in your work, cite it as below."
title: "MarketTickStreamer.jl: provider-agnostic tick-by-tick market data acquisition and paced replay in Julia"
abstract: >-
  A Julia package that acquires tick-by-tick market data for scientific
  analysis: live WebSocket streaming, historical backfill from paginated
  REST or the venue's daily dumps behind one provider-agnostic interface,
  import of Nasdaq TotalView-ITCH 5.0 and IEX HIST day files, an
  append-only crash-only raw layer with per-session provenance, compaction
  to per-symbol per-day CSV or Arrow on the venue's own calendar, and paced
  replay of a recording, or following of a running session from another
  process, into the same channel type the live source produces. Adapters
  ship for Alpaca (US equities) and Binance (crypto spot). Analysis
  pipelines couple to a capture through a documented channel contract and a
  documented file contract; the package implements no estimators.
type: software
